WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.333 --> 00:00:07.433
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

00:00:09.433 --> 00:00:13.267
Okay, I didn't get a good look;
so the real question here:

00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:16.800
Is that helicopter being
piloted by that Barney guy?

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.300
Actually, hold that. Can I stay down here?

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:23.500
No, I'd have to eat the aliens.
That's not fucking happening.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.267
So, uh... hey, I have an idea.

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:28.533
This is the most basic ruse there is

00:00:28.533 --> 00:00:31.267
but these cops seem to have
more bullets than brains.

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:32.967
HEY! OVER HERE! I'M A LIGHTNING BUG!

00:00:32.967 --> 00:00:34.900
[machine gun fire]
That's good! That's good!

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:38.267
Just keep firing there! Keep
firing! Maybe you got me!

00:00:38.267 --> 00:00:40.167
C'mon...shit!

00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:41.467
...home base...

00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:43.967
[machine gun fire]
Oh! You bastard!

00:00:43.967 --> 00:00:45.033
Okay, my turn!

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:48.500
I don't think that did anything.

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:52.467
Well you win this time,
Barney...if that IS your real name.

00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:56.067
Okay, I don't KNOW that's him,
but I sort of sense it, y'know?

00:00:56.067 --> 00:00:59.467
I mean, he sent me in the
canals, I know that much.

00:00:59.467 --> 00:01:03.300
Wow. More bullets. I really could
just stay here firing at him,

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.600
but I think that's what he wants.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:08.300
See this is what makes
me the last man standing,

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.467
because I'm not just standing here.

00:01:10.467 --> 00:01:12.500
Well, that and being bullet-proof...

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:15.233
...except for my head! Kleiner...

00:01:15.233 --> 00:01:19.367
Okay, so I guess I really am
trying to get lost at this point

00:01:19.367 --> 00:01:22.167
because if I can't find
me, they can't find me.

00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:26.367
Well, that's actually not really true,
but there's probably a correlation.

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:28.267
There's a lot of junk down here.

00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:31.133
[straining]

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:33.933
I don't know much about this society,

00:01:33.933 --> 00:01:38.767
but I think they make it too hard to do
trash pickup. Maybe they charge too much,

00:01:38.767 --> 00:01:42.833
or knowing this place, you have to present
three forms of ID to throw away a can.

00:01:42.833 --> 00:01:47.000
Oh! Maybe that's what that cop was
doing--making sure I was certified!

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:50.000
DRINKING SODA COULD'VE SAVED MY LIFE!

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.233
Okay, this is boarded off. That's good.

00:01:52.233 --> 00:01:56.167
If I'm lucky, this won't be on a blueprint
so they'll think I've ceased to exist.

00:01:57.133 --> 00:01:58.300
What the fuck? MAN: Get in here, quick!

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:00.167
[stuttering]
MAN: Civil Protection is onto us.

00:02:00.167 --> 00:02:02.267
MAN: We're tearing up the
Railroad, covering our tracks.

00:02:02.267 --> 00:02:05.233
Well, you didn't try to kill me...

00:02:05.233 --> 00:02:09.033
So you've passed the first test.
One of many.

00:02:09.033 --> 00:02:10.567
MAN: Looks like you're going
to be the last one through.

00:02:10.567 --> 00:02:11.533
Uh, yeah.

00:02:11.533 --> 00:02:13.133
MAN: Be glad you're not the
guy they're looking for.

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:15.667
Yeah, fuck him, right? MAN: Poor
bastard wouldn't stand a chance.

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:18.400
MAN: Sounds like they're calling
in every CP unit in City 17.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:20.200
No, they have a few less units now.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.167
MAN: Now they're flooding the
areas up ahead with manhacks.

00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:23.000
Yeah, what does that mean?

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.067
MAN: Better get going before
they sweep through here.

00:02:25.067 --> 00:02:26.967
MAN: OH SHIT! TOO LATE!

00:02:26.967 --> 00:02:28.800
Yeah, welcome to my world.

00:02:29.867 --> 00:02:30.767
What the hell?

00:02:32.867 --> 00:02:33.533
WAH!

00:02:35.633 --> 00:02:37.867
OKAY, I DON'T WANT TO HIT YOU, BUT...!

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:44.367
Hey! That's great! I don't
think I shot you even once!

00:02:44.367 --> 00:02:45.567
MAN: Thanks for your help!

00:02:45.567 --> 00:02:47.800
You...are welcome.

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.967
MAN: Look, it isn't safe here.

00:02:49.967 --> 00:02:51.100
Yeah, I guessed that.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.233
MAN: I'll give you some supplies to keep
you going, then you really gotta go.

00:02:53.233 --> 00:02:56.967
Oh supplies, huh? I like supplies.

00:02:56.967 --> 00:02:58.900
Do you have any drugs?

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:02.733
Like opioids, specifically. I'm not too
picky right now, just not stimulants.

00:03:02.733 --> 00:03:06.133
I'm-- Oh, that's just for you, huh?

00:03:06.133 --> 00:03:07.867
Well...I don't blame you,

00:03:07.867 --> 00:03:12.133
but if you get me high, you pass all
the tests. We can skip the rest of it.

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:15.133
What's up here? This is where
you keep the good stuff, right?

00:03:15.133 --> 00:03:16.967
Oh, more ammo.

00:03:16.967 --> 00:03:22.967
Wow! Okay. I think I've literally seen
more ammo packs than soda cans by now.

00:03:22.967 --> 00:03:26.133
This is kind of cozy...
for living in a sewer.

00:03:26.133 --> 00:03:26.833
A pot!

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:30.200
I'd care more if you had food.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:34.367
Actually, I'm not that hungry now.
My stomach's feeling...challenged.

00:03:34.367 --> 00:03:38.400
Okay, the big boxes. What do
we have here? Supply time.

00:03:39.067 --> 00:03:39.900
Empty.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:41.800
What?

00:03:43.067 --> 00:03:46.600
They're empty! They're all
empty! There's nothing here!

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:48.067
Man, you're high!

00:03:48.067 --> 00:03:49.467
YOU SAID I COULD HAVE SUPPLIES,

00:03:49.467 --> 00:03:52.933
BUT ALL YOU HAVE IS AN EMPTY
POT THAT YOU WEAR ON YOUR HEAD!

00:03:52.933 --> 00:03:55.500
Okay, you do have bullets;
I'll give you that,

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:58.033
although I don't know
if I can carry any more.

00:03:58.033 --> 00:03:59.367
What is this?

00:03:59.367 --> 00:04:00.467
[growls]

00:04:00.467 --> 00:04:03.900
Ah, okay. The small package.
This has got to be it, right?

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:05.200
Yeah, this looks legit.

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:08.733
Are you kidding me? It's empty.

00:04:08.733 --> 00:04:11.767
"Yes, please help yourself to
my wide supply of empty boxes

00:04:11.767 --> 00:04:13.433
"and a glowing breathalyzer.

00:04:13.433 --> 00:04:15.867
"And bullets. I naturally have lots of those

00:04:15.867 --> 00:04:18.133
"because I have no gun to shoot them with."

00:04:18.133 --> 00:04:19.767
I think his mind's baked.

00:04:19.767 --> 00:04:23.633
He's just gathering random
things and calling them supplies.

00:04:23.633 --> 00:04:25.000
And lives in a sewer.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:28.400
Listen, Johnny Appleseed,
you're low on supplies.

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:33.867
Oh, you're having a bad trip. I can
see that. Okay, I'll go easy on you.

00:04:33.867 --> 00:04:40.200
Oh yeah. So this is a manhack, huh? It's
just a flying circular saw, isn't it?

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:45.167
This isn't what I thought at all! This
is redneck technology! It's obvious.

00:04:45.167 --> 00:04:47.533
I can tell you right now
this was invented by

00:04:47.533 --> 00:04:51.233
some guy duct-taping a circular saw
to a remote controlled helicopter

00:04:51.233 --> 00:04:53.133
to keep people off his property.

00:04:53.133 --> 00:04:54.000
["Good luck out there!"]

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.033
Wait, what? You're not coming?

00:04:56.033 --> 00:04:59.367
You just said I'm the last man
through, you're shutting this down.

00:04:59.367 --> 00:05:02.800
The cops are not far behind me.
You think they won't shoot you if--

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:05.267
Okay, forget it. I don't have time for this.

00:05:05.267 --> 00:05:07.033
Well, that was nice of him
to give me the bullets,

00:05:07.033 --> 00:05:10.933
but considering how plentiful those
are, plus he held out on the drugs,

00:05:10.933 --> 00:05:13.300
I think that makes us even.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:15.467
[manhacks whirring]
That's not a happy sound.

00:05:15.467 --> 00:05:16.467
AH HAH!

00:05:18.967 --> 00:05:20.567
They're not even that fast.

00:05:23.267 --> 00:05:29.000
You are no match against me and
your nemesis: the chainlink fence.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:31.067
Whoa! Spring hinge.

00:05:31.067 --> 00:05:33.133
They're probably using a simple AI:

00:05:33.133 --> 00:05:36.533
just fly at anything human-shaped
that shows up in infrared.

00:05:36.533 --> 00:05:38.067
That's how--Oop!

00:05:38.067 --> 00:05:42.100
I'm not even sure if they can process
corners but why learn the hard way?

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:43.900
Chain-link shields up!

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:44.867
[explosion]

00:05:44.867 --> 00:05:47.667
WOW! Did they blow themselves up?

00:05:47.667 --> 00:05:49.433
How did they set that on fire?

00:05:49.433 --> 00:05:53.333
I'm not impressed by these things. I
think they just fly in a straight line.

00:05:53.333 --> 00:05:55.000
Yep! All gone!

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:58.133
All that technology going
into something stupid.

00:05:58.133 --> 00:06:01.767
I mean, sure, they're dangerous
but not very effective.

00:06:01.767 --> 00:06:03.133
Okay, check the corners...!

00:06:04.833 --> 00:06:10.933
If your top-end robotic assault device can
be defeated with a baseball bat every time,

00:06:10.933 --> 00:06:13.200
well that kind of says it all, doesn't it?

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:17.533
Okay, I'll take a few more
bullets since you insist.

00:06:17.533 --> 00:06:20.767
But yeah, the engineering
behind that isn't lost on me,

00:06:20.767 --> 00:06:22.600
it's just--Okay, wait.

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:26.167
I don't see anyone. Seems calm.

00:06:26.167 --> 00:06:28.033
I'm opening the door.

00:06:28.033 --> 00:06:30.833
I'm walking through the door--God dammit.

00:06:30.833 --> 00:06:31.867
Keep going--Nope!

00:06:34.767 --> 00:06:39.500
I'd rather be theorizing! The
expectations are so different.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:42.733
[manhack whirring]
Oop! Now I'm a street physicist.

00:06:42.733 --> 00:06:44.233
Thwarted again!

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.667
Okay, wait. Let's see this. Let's see this.

00:06:47.667 --> 00:06:50.867
Yep! Straight line right at the fence!

00:06:51.733 --> 00:06:53.567
Yeah, keep coming, I'm here!

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:01.033
I've got the bullets! Let's do this!

00:07:01.033 --> 00:07:01.933
Oh, more!

00:07:02.967 --> 00:07:04.867
Yeah! Let's get this out of the way!

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:10.333
Any more? I'm happy to shoot more robots
that can't hurt me. That's not a problem.

00:07:10.333 --> 00:07:12.733
Okay, I'm opening the door.

00:07:12.733 --> 00:07:15.300
I'm walking through the door.

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:19.033
I SAID, "I'M WALKING THROUGH THE DOOR!"

00:07:19.033 --> 00:07:22.533
I guess they ran out of manhacks. Good.

00:07:22.533 --> 00:07:26.667
Yeah, being a street physicist is
kind of a downgrade from where I was.

00:07:26.667 --> 00:07:29.733
It's mostly just kinetic
energy and collisions.

00:07:29.733 --> 00:07:30.933
Yeah, see?

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:32.700
Whoa!

00:07:34.667 --> 00:07:37.867
So where do I--? Hey, I
think I'll shut the door?

00:07:37.867 --> 00:07:40.300
That should send them
back to the drawing board.

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:44.267
I'd feel better about this route if I
could've stayed underground the whole time.

00:07:44.267 --> 00:07:49.367
Isn't that the point? To not
be seen? I'm really acing that.

00:07:49.367 --> 00:07:54.633
Oh! Here we go! It would be nice to
throw them off my trail for once.

00:07:54.633 --> 00:07:59.233
They probably don't expect me to climb
into a ventilation shaft. I wouldn't.

00:07:59.233 --> 00:08:01.567
That's never really been
a lifestyle choice...

00:08:02.333 --> 00:08:04.100
...so much as a necessity.

00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:06.200
I swear, I haven't seen
one fork in the path--

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:07.333
Oh shit!

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:11.000
AH! FUCK THAT HURT!

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:12.200
Why are you...?

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:17.133
AH! MY FACE! MY BEAUTIFUL FACE!
WHAT HAVE YOU DONE TO ME?!

00:08:17.133 --> 00:08:18.400
FUCKIN' SAW BLADE--

00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:20.167
[raging]

00:08:20.167 --> 00:08:23.333
PIECE OF SHIT, OVER-ENGINEERED
ROBOT RAT TRAP...!

00:08:23.333 --> 00:08:26.400
THERE'S NO OPENING! IT REALLY WAS
JUST SITTING HERE TO KILL RATS!

00:08:27.533 --> 00:08:31.867
Yeah, let's throw in AI, propulsion
system, gyroscopes, infrared sensors,

00:08:31.867 --> 00:08:35.233
and some next-gen battery tech
in there so we can kill rats.

00:08:35.233 --> 00:08:39.300
This had to be a Department of Defense
contract. It's got all the signs.

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:41.533
[lock jiggles]
Oh, come ON!

00:08:41.533 --> 00:08:42.400
[growls]

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:43.967
Anything in the boxes?

00:08:44.967 --> 00:08:46.900
Yes!

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:48.233
No.

00:08:48.233 --> 00:08:51.533
All this ammo lying around. I
still haven't figured that out.

00:08:51.533 --> 00:08:54.600
I figure this must be
somebody's dream come true:

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:58.933
Not being able to walk for five minutes
without tripping over a canister of bullets.

00:08:58.933 --> 00:09:01.533
Not sure who or why though.

00:09:01.533 --> 00:09:02.933
Yeah, I'm full.

00:09:02.933 --> 00:09:04.533
A barred window.

00:09:04.533 --> 00:09:06.867
Is this a dungeon? Maybe.

00:09:06.867 --> 00:09:09.200
This is Europe...or Russia.

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:11.400
Back the way I came in!

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:14.033
So yeah, I guess manhacks are effective

00:09:14.033 --> 00:09:19.267
if you're spread prone in a vent and
have trouble moving both your arms.

00:09:19.267 --> 00:09:21.867
For all I know, Black Mesa developed these,

00:09:21.867 --> 00:09:22.633
because--Shit!

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:24.800
Did he see me?

00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:26.933
He might have.

00:09:26.933 --> 00:09:28.467
Well...

00:09:28.467 --> 00:09:28.833
What if--

00:09:30.367 --> 00:09:32.000
Yes. He did.

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:33.833
Haa, that's loud.

00:09:33.833 --> 00:09:37.367
That's okay. I think I'm
going half deaf by now anyway.

00:09:37.367 --> 00:09:40.100
Boy, they're on my ASS, huh!

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:42.533
That guy was, what, a minute behind me?

00:09:42.533 --> 00:09:47.733
Wait, the door's still shut. Did he do
that? Or did he come up from the bottom?

00:09:47.733 --> 00:09:49.167
THEY'RE IN THE WALLS!

00:09:49.167 --> 00:09:50.733
Wait, no, that's aliens.

00:09:52.433 --> 00:09:55.400
Okay, I don't see anyone.

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:58.233
Hmm. Could he fit through there?

00:09:58.233 --> 00:10:00.100
No, I don't think so.

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:01.900
So this is my best lead.

00:10:01.900 --> 00:10:04.533
Well, I'll just take things nice and easy.

00:10:04.533 --> 00:10:05.400
Ba-HO-HO-HO...!

00:10:07.733 --> 00:10:08.900
YOU SCARED ME!

00:10:12.067 --> 00:10:14.800
"No, Gordon, people aren't
flying down from the sky

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:19.333
"to come kill you like some sort of
fallen angel! You're just being paranoid!"

00:10:19.333 --> 00:10:22.100
Yeah, who am I to argue with dead people?

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:24.267
Oh! A machine gun!

00:10:24.267 --> 00:10:28.733
This is just what the doctor
ordered for my itchy trigger finger.

00:10:28.733 --> 00:10:31.033
Now it doesn't need to twitch so much.

00:10:31.033 --> 00:10:35.000
Hup! Yeah, more! Join the
club! This is an open invite.

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:36.033
[distant wood cracking]

00:10:36.033 --> 00:10:37.367
What the fuck was that?

00:10:38.667 --> 00:10:39.867
Well...

00:10:39.867 --> 00:10:42.200
I've got a machine gun!

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:45.933
I get the feeling that's going to
be my answer to a lot of questions.

00:10:45.933 --> 00:10:46.900
Uh...

00:10:48.533 --> 00:10:52.000
So this is a dead end?
But this is the only way.

00:10:53.567 --> 00:10:54.967
Am I missing something?

00:10:54.967 --> 00:10:58.100
Is there a trampoline I'm
supposed to bounce out of here on?

00:10:58.100 --> 00:11:01.533
Why would there be all this
infrastructure just to lead to nothing?!

00:11:01.533 --> 00:11:04.300
It's all barred off! What the fuck?!

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:05.600
HELLO!

00:11:11.667 --> 00:11:13.200
Well...

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:14.967
I have a machine gun!

